# Raw CogVideoX output. The generator writes its first frame and its unencoded
# clip here as it goes, so this folder fills with work-in-progress that should
# not ship. Finished clips get encoded for the web and moved to assets/video/
# deliberately; nothing lands on the site by accident.
assets/video/kitchen/

# Dish renders: 768x1024 PNG masters, ~1.5MB each. The site loads the derived
# jpgs (assets/img/dish/*.jpg thumbnails, assets/img/reel/*.jpg stills), which
# scripts/derive-dish-assets.py rebuilds from these. Thirty megabytes of PNG has no business
# in a shop's website repo.
assets/img/dish/*.png

# Era renders for the food story: 1152x768 PNG masters. The page loads the
# jpgs that scripts/derive-food-images.py builds from these.
assets/img/food/*.png
